WEBVTT

00:02.045 --> 00:04.005
[Narrator] Previously on lost:

00:04.088 --> 00:05.173
[Wet thud]

00:06.925 --> 00:10.678
You killed Naomi!
— she wants her people to come here.

00:10.762 --> 00:13.556
And trust me, when they do,
we had better be far away from here.

00:13.640 --> 00:16.100
If you want to live,
you need to come with me.

00:27.320 --> 00:29.072
[Jack] Who are you?
— Daniel Faraday.

00:29.155 --> 00:30.573
I'm here to rescue you.

00:30.657 --> 00:33.826
[Naomi] This is the team? These are
the wrong people for this mission.

00:33.910 --> 00:36.746
None of them have field experience,
military training.

00:36.829 --> 00:39.832
You can't drop them in unprotected.
There's only so much I can do.

00:39.916 --> 00:42.543
Where's the chopper?
Where did it crash?

00:42.627 --> 00:46.256
What kind of pilot do you think I am?
I put her down safe and sound.

00:46.339 --> 00:48.925
Get up. You're coming with us.
— we need to stay where we are

00:49.008 --> 00:51.761
so they can find us.
— see, there's your problem.

00:51.844 --> 00:53.429
We don't want to be found.

00:53.513 --> 00:56.266
You want to know why we're here?
I'll tell you why.

00:56.349 --> 00:58.851
We're here for Benjamin Linus.

00:58.935 --> 01:01.104
Now where is he?

01:21.457 --> 01:24.460
[Jack] Did Ben mention knowing
anyone off the island?

01:24.544 --> 01:26.796
You're sure of that?
— this is real simple.

01:26.879 --> 01:28.965
Do you know where he is, or don't you?

01:29.048 --> 01:32.051
What do you want with him?
— I want to locate him.

01:32.135 --> 01:35.054
The people who hired me told me
his name's Benjamin Linus.

01:35.138 --> 01:37.598
They gave me this picture,
that's all he told me.

01:37.682 --> 01:40.310
They said find him.
And for what they're paying me,

01:40.393 --> 01:42.228
I don't need to know anything else.

01:43.104 --> 01:44.439
Do you?

01:46.065 --> 01:50.153
[Jack] You want Ben? Ok,
he's with Locke and your friend...

01:50.236 --> 01:51.946
[Miles] Charlotte. — Charlotte.

01:52.030 --> 01:54.741
[Jack] Locke's got her too.
We know where he's heading.

01:54.824 --> 01:58.661
[Miles] Locke's the guy that killed
Naomi. Give me back my gun, Shephard.

01:58.745 --> 02:01.205
[Jack] You want your gun back,
I want answers.

02:01.289 --> 02:03.958
[Miles] You don't trust me,
I don't trust you.

02:04.042 --> 02:08.671
In fact, you're supposed to be dead.
Am I asking a billion questions? No.

02:08.755 --> 02:11.758
We both have the same problem,
this Locke guy.

02:11.841 --> 02:15.303
Even if Locke has your friend,
you can't waltz in there and grab her.

02:15.386 --> 02:17.847
They're armed.
— how about that? So are we.

02:17.930 --> 02:20.767
Why don't we move out...?
— you're not going anwvhere.

02:20.850 --> 02:24.354
Will that helicopter fly?
— It's what she does.

02:24.437 --> 02:27.440
Then you can take me to your ship.
— Sayid, wait a second.

02:27.523 --> 02:30.735
We did call these people
to get us off this island, didn't we?

02:35.073 --> 02:38.034
I burned a lot of fuel coming in.
I can't carry much weight.

02:38.117 --> 02:40.536
I'll take three of you.
— In case you zoned out

02:40.620 --> 02:44.207
while tweezing your goatee, one
of these yahoos took Charlotte prisoner.

02:44.290 --> 02:46.376
I can bring her back safely.

02:50.463 --> 02:54.342
And if I do...
Will you take me to the ship?

02:55.802 --> 02:57.053
Absolutely.

02:59.555 --> 03:01.766
You bring Charlotte back safe...

03:03.142 --> 03:05.436
And I will take you off this island.

03:20.952 --> 03:23.454
[Golf cart approaching]

03:27.917 --> 03:29.919
Good morning. — good morning.

03:30.002 --> 03:33.506
It's a long walk to the next hole.
Do you need a ride?

03:33.589 --> 03:36.259
Thank you, but no.
My ball is right here.

03:36.342 --> 03:39.137
You're the first person I've seen
out here all morning.

03:40.471 --> 03:43.724
I believe we're paying quite a premium
for that kind of privacy.

03:43.808 --> 03:46.018
Indeed, we are.

03:49.147 --> 03:51.357
Is this your first time
in the Seychelles?

03:54.318 --> 03:56.487
Uh—uh. I'd use the five iron.

03:57.530 --> 03:59.282
I think I'll stick with the seven.

03:59.365 --> 04:04.120
Tell you what. Fifty Euros says mine
goes closer to the pin with a five.

04:07.623 --> 04:08.749
Let's make it 100.

04:08.833 --> 04:10.710
[Speaks foreign language]

04:11.711 --> 04:14.338
Amazing, huh? How we wager.

04:14.422 --> 04:16.340
Makes just about anything more fun.

04:36.110 --> 04:39.655
So, what do you do for a living,
my friend?

04:40.573 --> 04:43.242
I do nothing. — nothing?

04:43.326 --> 04:45.119
Doesn't pay for a vacation here.

04:45.995 --> 04:48.164
I was the recipient
of a large settlement.

04:48.247 --> 04:50.917
Corporate merger?
— actually a plane crash.

04:53.211 --> 04:55.671
Oceanic airlines flight 815.

04:55.755 --> 04:57.757
I'm Sayid Jarrah...

04:58.424 --> 05:00.426
One of the oceanic six.

05:03.721 --> 05:05.473
Ah, that's...

05:05.556 --> 05:07.558
That's amazing.

05:08.684 --> 05:10.937
I remember reading all about it.

05:11.771 --> 05:13.439
Take your shot, my friend.

05:26.619 --> 05:29.580
It appears you were right
about the five iron.

05:30.289 --> 05:32.542
Well, uh...

05:33.543 --> 05:36.295
Enjoy your round.
Don't worry about the wager.

05:37.380 --> 05:40.216
It's all in good fun.
— no, you won. Allow me to pay you.

05:40.299 --> 05:43.094
It's fine, thank you.
— I insist, Mr. Avellino.

05:46.973 --> 05:47.974
[Avellino grunts]

06:16.335 --> 06:18.879
[People chattering]

06:39.442 --> 06:41.152
[Speaks German]

06:50.995 --> 06:52.872
[Speaks German]

06:53.414 --> 06:55.791
"Is it free?" Was the full extent
of my German.

06:58.669 --> 07:00.963
What are you looking for?

07:01.047 --> 07:04.050
I love Europe.
Everyone speaks English.

07:04.133 --> 07:07.470
I'm looking for potsdamer platz.
— you don't need a map.

07:07.553 --> 07:09.972
It's one block down,
right across the street.

07:10.056 --> 07:12.016
Thank you.

07:16.354 --> 07:18.814
I'm Elsa.

07:18.898 --> 07:20.650
Sayid.

07:21.359 --> 07:22.693
[Man speaking German]

07:22.777 --> 07:24.654
Could I have an Espresso, please?

07:24.737 --> 07:26.155
[Man speaks German]

07:26.238 --> 07:28.699
What sort of business
brings you to Berlin?

07:28.783 --> 07:30.409
I'm a headhunter.

07:30.493 --> 07:31.994
A corporate recruiter.

07:33.329 --> 07:36.707
And what do you do?
— my employer is an economist.

07:36.791 --> 07:39.251
He works in emerging markets.

07:39.335 --> 07:42.004
Actually, I don't really understand
what he does,

07:42.088 --> 07:45.424
which doesn't matter
since all I do is shop for him.

07:46.759 --> 07:48.469
And if this goes off,

07:48.552 --> 07:51.472
I'm at his side instantly.

07:51.555 --> 07:55.017
Which is wonderful, since he's only
in Berlin once or twice a year.

07:55.101 --> 07:58.771
Which is why you're enjoying
a luxuriously long midday coffee.

08:03.943 --> 08:05.611
[Speaks German]

08:20.960 --> 08:22.545
Know you from somewhere?

08:23.587 --> 08:26.006
I'll tell you exactly where
you know me from...

08:27.758 --> 08:29.510
If you let me take you to dinner.

08:37.143 --> 08:38.811
Umm...

08:43.274 --> 08:46.485
This is the restaurant
you're taking me tonight. 8:00.

08:47.987 --> 08:50.406
Well, if you can find it.

09:05.045 --> 09:08.090
[Dialing]

09:08.174 --> 09:10.092
[Man] Hello? — I made contact.

09:10.176 --> 09:11.510
[Man] Good.

09:29.653 --> 09:30.988
Take a look at this.

09:32.531 --> 09:34.366
Naomi had it with her.

09:36.035 --> 09:37.995
She was looking for Desmond.

09:40.539 --> 09:44.043
Whatever their real agenda is
it's clear they're not sharing it.

09:44.126 --> 09:46.295
Maybe Desmond
can shed some light on this.

09:48.214 --> 09:50.966
[Jack] How long would it take
to get to the beach and back?

09:51.050 --> 09:52.301
[Juliet] Couple of hours.

09:53.719 --> 09:55.387
You mind?

09:55.471 --> 09:57.473
Anything I can do to help.

09:58.724 --> 09:59.809
[Jack] Sayid.

10:02.603 --> 10:04.271
So how are we gonna do this?

10:04.355 --> 10:07.608
You know the best candidate
for this kind of mission.

10:07.691 --> 10:11.320
And what kind of mission is that?
— I'll make Locke release Charlotte,

10:11.403 --> 10:14.156
and I'm going to do it
without any bloodshed.

10:14.240 --> 10:16.700
As opposed to the way I'd do it?

10:17.409 --> 10:20.329
The last time you encountered him
you put a gun to his head

10:20.412 --> 10:21.747
and pulled the trigger.

10:21.831 --> 10:23.833
That's not good diplomacy.

10:24.583 --> 10:26.335
Hey, Jarrah.

10:27.044 --> 10:29.672
You think you're going
after Charlotte without me?

10:29.755 --> 10:31.131
Of course not.

10:31.215 --> 10:33.801
Oh. Well, good.

10:35.761 --> 10:37.096
Is there anything else?

10:39.181 --> 10:42.518
Yeah. Give me my gun back.
— we leave in ten minutes.

10:47.606 --> 10:49.775
[Panting]

10:49.859 --> 10:52.111
Ready to give us a name, gizmo?

10:53.404 --> 10:56.490
He's not gonna tell you who
his spy is on their boat, James.

10:56.574 --> 10:57.992
[Sawyer] Yeah, and why not?

10:58.075 --> 11:00.494
[Locke] That's the only thing
keeping him alive.

11:00.578 --> 11:01.662
Here's an idea.

11:01.745 --> 11:04.373
Why don't we take a gun,
point it to his big toe

11:04.456 --> 11:06.584
and send that little piggy to market?

11:06.667 --> 11:10.880
And if he still doesn't want to tell us,
we'll move on to the roast beef.

11:10.963 --> 11:14.174
Why don't we do that?
— then we'd have to carry him.

11:33.944 --> 11:36.614
[Aaron crying]
— [Claire] John, how much further is it?

11:36.697 --> 11:39.700
I need to feed Aaron.
— It should be here, the cabin.

11:41.243 --> 11:43.829
Maybe we got turned around.
Could be anwvhere.

11:43.913 --> 11:44.914
No, it was here.

11:44.997 --> 11:47.583
What's in this cabin
that's so important?

11:47.666 --> 11:50.711
John's looking for somebody
to tell him what to do next.

12:00.930 --> 12:02.932
I guess I was mistaken.
It doesn't...

12:03.015 --> 12:05.684
It doesn't matter.
Plan's the same. We keep moving.

12:05.768 --> 12:07.436
The barracks aren't far.

12:07.519 --> 12:11.607
If her team is with Jack's group,
they know we're going to the barracks.

12:11.690 --> 12:13.609
Yeah, and red here was wearing a vest,

12:13.692 --> 12:16.779
which means her posse's gonna come
expecting a gunfight.

12:16.862 --> 12:19.448
If all they want is her,
maybe we should let her go.

12:19.531 --> 12:23.619
I thought we were just gonna go hide.
Why do we need to take prisoners?

12:23.702 --> 12:25.454
Because she'll be valuable.

12:25.537 --> 12:28.791
How is she gonna be valuable?
— he means as a hostage, love.

12:30.459 --> 12:33.379
No, this is not what I signed up for.
— what did you sign up for?

12:33.462 --> 12:37.383
If we let her go, they'll look at it
as a sign of good faith.

12:37.466 --> 12:39.635
They'll look at it
as an act of foolishness.

12:39.718 --> 12:41.637
I'm trying to come up with a compromise.

12:41.720 --> 12:43.722
We're beyond compromise.

12:43.806 --> 12:46.684
And right now, Hugo,
I'm making the decisions.

12:48.143 --> 12:50.771
Is that going to be a problem for you?

12:57.945 --> 12:59.697
[Kate] Kinda sucks, huh?

13:01.281 --> 13:02.491
What's that?

13:04.034 --> 13:06.036
Being told not to come along.

13:08.622 --> 13:10.624
Now you know what it feels like
to be me.

13:11.917 --> 13:14.503
Does that mean I should
wait 20 minutes and go anwvay?

13:14.586 --> 13:17.965
[Both laughing] — touche.

13:25.848 --> 13:27.850
You should go with them, Kate.

13:29.935 --> 13:31.729
You're serious? — yeah.

13:35.274 --> 13:37.276
What, don't you trust Sayid?

13:38.110 --> 13:39.528
I don't trust Locke.

13:41.780 --> 13:45.075
What's preventing him from doing to me
what he did to Naomi?

13:48.495 --> 13:49.705
Sawyer won't let him.

14:02.801 --> 14:04.094
You got room for one more?

14:05.429 --> 14:06.930
Oh, yeah, she gets a gun.

14:08.432 --> 14:11.935
The gun's a last resort, Kate.
— you give Locke that same speech?

14:12.019 --> 14:14.438
Hey! Let's move out.

14:23.363 --> 14:25.824
This guy, Sayid, where is he from?

14:27.785 --> 14:29.286
Iraq.

14:29.369 --> 14:31.038
Iraq?

14:32.456 --> 14:35.292
So he's just gonna go
and work everything out?

14:35.375 --> 14:37.377
What was he, a diplomat?

14:42.508 --> 14:44.134
No, he was a torturer.

14:56.146 --> 14:58.857
Naomi, were you close to her?

14:58.941 --> 15:01.110
Nope. Met her on the boat.

15:01.193 --> 15:03.946
You don't seem particularly affected
by her death.

15:04.029 --> 15:06.740
Sure, I'm affected. She was hot,
and I dug her accent.

15:06.824 --> 15:07.866
Nice.

15:08.617 --> 15:12.079
And this woman, Charlotte.
You don't care about her, do you?

15:12.162 --> 15:15.624
Define "care."
— so much for camaraderie.

15:15.707 --> 15:19.044
Who's the one going after one
of their crash buddies with guns?

15:19.128 --> 15:21.463
Actually, I do care about Locke.

15:21.547 --> 15:26.051
Maybe you can tell me how he managed to
split your happy little family in half.

15:29.346 --> 15:33.100
There was a fundamental debate whether
your people came to rescue us...

15:33.183 --> 15:34.351
Or kill us.

15:35.811 --> 15:37.563
Which side did you land on?

15:39.356 --> 15:41.567
I'll let you know when I decide.

15:42.985 --> 15:46.071
[Jazz music playing]

15:48.490 --> 15:50.492
You look fantastic.

15:53.162 --> 15:55.622
This is why I wanted to take you
to the opera.

16:01.086 --> 16:04.298
If a man can't wear his tuxedo
by the fifth date, why bother?

16:22.983 --> 16:24.318
You know what?

16:26.862 --> 16:28.614
I'm not bringing it.

16:29.281 --> 16:32.326
If tonight's the night he calls,
so be it.

16:37.497 --> 16:38.790
I'll carry it.

16:39.666 --> 16:42.753
If he does call,
I don't want you fired over me.

16:43.962 --> 16:46.882
You should tell your employer
there is newer technology.

16:47.633 --> 16:50.052
Oh, I've tried.
He's very old—fashioned.

16:50.135 --> 16:52.554
You know how bosses can be.

16:53.972 --> 16:55.641
Do you have a boss?

16:56.433 --> 16:58.477
Everyone has a boss, Elsa.

17:01.480 --> 17:03.482
Come on, we don't want to be late.

17:06.026 --> 17:07.903
Why are you still here?

17:07.986 --> 17:12.157
I mean, when we met, you said
you would be in Berlin for one week.

17:14.159 --> 17:17.371
The job I'm on is proving harder
to accomplish than I thought.

17:22.668 --> 17:23.794
Right.

17:24.920 --> 17:28.674
I was hoping it was because of me.

17:31.843 --> 17:32.886
[Laughs]

17:39.685 --> 17:41.061
Let's go.

17:41.144 --> 17:42.479
Strauss awaits.

18:20.767 --> 18:24.813
What's his story?
— Daniel? Couldn't tell you.

18:24.896 --> 18:27.024
Half the stuff he says
goes way over my head.

18:27.107 --> 18:28.900
The other half goes way, way over.

18:29.818 --> 18:32.237
Uh, frank, can I...?

18:32.321 --> 18:35.657
Sorry to interrupt. May I please
use the phone just for a sec?

18:35.741 --> 18:38.035
For what?
— I want to call Regina on the boat.

18:38.118 --> 18:40.996
Since we're waiting
maybe I can just try to...

18:41.079 --> 18:43.707
What is it, Daniel?
— I'd like to do an experiment.

18:43.790 --> 18:45.042
Just... — ok.

18:45.125 --> 18:47.836
You just keep it to that
science stuff, all right?

18:47.919 --> 18:50.589
If minkowski gets on there,
hang up right away.

18:50.672 --> 18:52.466
Yeah, thank you, thank you.

18:52.841 --> 18:53.842
[Phone ringing]

18:53.925 --> 18:55.469
[Woman] Hello? — Regina?

18:55.552 --> 18:57.304
Hey, hi, it's Dan. Hang on.

18:58.096 --> 19:00.223
Can you hear me? — yeah.

19:00.307 --> 19:02.100
Yeah? Ok. Hang on.

19:02.184 --> 19:04.811
I'm... oh... yes.

19:04.895 --> 19:08.565
I am all set here. I have a fix.
Are you locked in?

19:08.648 --> 19:12.361
Getting your signal pretty clear.
— ok, great, then.

19:15.030 --> 19:16.406
Fire the payload.

19:16.490 --> 19:17.991
[Regina] Payload away.

19:18.075 --> 19:21.578
Don't sweat it. He does this kind
of stuff on the boat all the time.

19:24.831 --> 19:27.334
[Regina] Forty kilometers to beacon.

19:27.417 --> 19:29.753
Thirty—five kilometers to beacon.

19:29.836 --> 19:31.838
Thirty kilometers to beacon.

19:31.922 --> 19:34.299
Twenty—five kilometers to beacon.

19:34.383 --> 19:36.760
Twenty kilometers to beacon.

19:36.843 --> 19:39.554
Fifteen kilometers to beacon.

19:39.638 --> 19:42.682
Ten kilometers to beacon.
— Regina?

19:42.766 --> 19:44.893
Five kilometers to beacon.

19:44.976 --> 19:46.311
Zero.

19:46.395 --> 19:48.105
I don't have it.

19:48.188 --> 19:50.315
[Regina] That's weird.

19:51.983 --> 19:54.653
That is far more than weird.

20:17.092 --> 20:20.137
What's with the swing set?
These people had daycare?

20:20.220 --> 20:23.181
You think they're here yet?
— let's find out.

20:40.532 --> 20:43.326
[Pounding]

20:58.508 --> 21:01.261
[Pounding continues]
— it's coming from in there.

21:03.221 --> 21:04.264
[Cocks gun]

21:10.562 --> 21:12.731
[Muffled shouting]

21:24.910 --> 21:26.244
Hurley, what happened?

21:28.163 --> 21:29.289
They left me.

21:30.999 --> 21:35.045
Locke's gone off the reservation, man.
He took this one chick hostage.

21:35.128 --> 21:38.173
He said Walt was the one who
told him to kill the other chick.

21:38.256 --> 21:39.841
Walt? — dude, don't ask.

21:39.925 --> 21:44.012
I was trying to argue with him
so he would chill, but...

21:44.095 --> 21:47.015
How about you stop babbling?
Tell us what happened to them.

21:47.098 --> 21:48.600
Where are they?

21:49.476 --> 21:52.020
Who are you?
— where the hell did they go, tubby?

21:52.103 --> 21:55.440
Oh, awesome, the ship sent us
another Sawyer.

21:55.524 --> 21:57.150
Hurley, where did they go?

21:57.234 --> 22:00.362
Guess they were too busy tying me up
to tell me. I don't know.

22:00.445 --> 22:03.406
So they all left? All together?
— yeah. They were freaked.

22:03.490 --> 22:07.202
Locke said the people on the ship were
coming to rescue Charlotte and kill us.

22:07.285 --> 22:10.038
So... are you?

22:13.250 --> 22:14.501
Not yet.

22:16.545 --> 22:20.215
Did they say anything that suggested
where they were going?

22:20.298 --> 22:23.552
Locke said they were going
by Ben's house before they took off.

22:23.635 --> 22:24.844
Why would he go there?

22:24.928 --> 22:27.889
For all I know they could've
locked Ben in the closet too.

22:27.973 --> 22:29.182
Where's Ben's house?

22:35.939 --> 22:38.733
You mind if I ask you a question?
— shoot.

22:39.943 --> 22:41.987
Did the Red Sox really win the series?

22:42.070 --> 22:44.990
Hey, don't get me started
on that, all right?

22:45.865 --> 22:48.326
My dad's from the Bronx.
I bleed yankee blue.

22:50.328 --> 22:53.206
I can't believe it's been 100 days
since I've seen a game.

22:58.003 --> 23:00.922
[Distant buzzing]
— it's the payload.

23:01.006 --> 23:02.966
It's finally here.

23:12.100 --> 23:14.936
What is that? — it's a rocket.

23:15.020 --> 23:17.230
[Beeping]

23:19.899 --> 23:21.234
Oh, no.

23:26.448 --> 23:27.949
Thirty one minutes.

23:29.034 --> 23:30.535
Oh, no.

23:31.453 --> 23:32.662
This is not good.

23:35.582 --> 23:37.334
Your friends are back.

23:47.927 --> 23:49.471
[Desmond] Well...

23:51.723 --> 23:53.016
Look at that.

24:05.945 --> 24:08.865
Look for anything that might show
where they've gone.

24:08.948 --> 24:10.492
I'll start in here.

26:13.573 --> 26:15.575
Sayid!

26:19.537 --> 26:21.164
Don't worry, Kate's fine.

26:27.962 --> 26:29.380
Good job, Hugo.

26:30.632 --> 26:32.383
Sorry, dude.

26:36.221 --> 26:38.807
I'm sorry, Sayid. Nothing personal.

26:38.890 --> 26:42.185
Where's Locke?
— talking to that angry Chinese guy.

26:43.561 --> 26:45.480
I'm not going to hurt you, Hurley.

26:45.563 --> 26:47.774
Yeah. I saw you snap that guy's neck

26:47.857 --> 26:50.610
with that break—dancing thing
you do with your legs.

26:50.693 --> 26:52.111
I think I'll hang back here.

27:01.204 --> 27:03.164
Well...

27:03.248 --> 27:05.625
I guess they're running out
of jail space.

27:11.422 --> 27:14.175
I lost a dollar, you know.
— how'd you manage that?

27:14.259 --> 27:16.636
I bet John that you wouldn't be
stupid enough

27:16.719 --> 27:18.930
to fall for your friend as bait.

27:21.391 --> 27:23.643
What do you know about friendship?

27:23.726 --> 27:27.313
I know it's no use having friends
you can't trust.

27:35.405 --> 27:37.323
So I'm your prisoner?

27:38.074 --> 27:40.118
If that sort of thing turns you on.

27:48.626 --> 27:50.628
What are you doing here with Locke?

27:52.630 --> 27:54.716
I'm not with him.
— yeah, you are, James.

27:54.799 --> 27:57.135
What are you doing with Jack?
— I went with Jack

27:57.218 --> 27:59.512
because I believe he can
get us off this island.

28:03.808 --> 28:06.352
Then I guess that's the difference
between us.

28:09.480 --> 28:10.940
I ain't iookin' to leave.

28:12.108 --> 28:13.776
Why not?

28:17.155 --> 28:19.824
'Cause I ain't got nothing
back there for me.

28:20.992 --> 28:23.661
And what's here that's so much better?

28:25.121 --> 28:27.624
Why do you want to go back, Kate?

28:29.167 --> 28:32.587
Seem to recall you being shuttled off
to jail before we landed here.

28:35.465 --> 28:39.135
So if you think there's anything
waiting for you other than handcuffs,

28:39.218 --> 28:41.846
then you really don't know
how the world works.

28:44.349 --> 28:47.936
Look around us, freckles.
We've got roofs over our heads.

28:48.019 --> 28:51.856
Electricity, showers, beds.
— how long, Sawyer?

28:51.940 --> 28:54.734
How long do you think
we can play house?

29:00.406 --> 29:02.492
Why don't we find out?

29:21.427 --> 29:22.553
Iced tea.

29:29.394 --> 29:32.313
Thought you might be thirsty.
— I'm thirsty.

29:35.525 --> 29:37.777
I'm sorry about all the theatrics,

29:37.860 --> 29:40.405
but I didn't know
how many of you there'd be

29:40.488 --> 29:42.240
or whether you'd be armed.

29:42.323 --> 29:44.993
I had to cover my bases.

29:45.076 --> 29:46.953
What have you done with miles and Kate?

29:47.036 --> 29:50.415
Kate's with Sawyer,
and miles is somewhere else.

29:52.917 --> 29:54.127
He's fine.

29:54.210 --> 29:57.630
All I did was ask him some questions.
— did he answer any?

29:57.714 --> 30:00.008
No.
— did you have more luck with the woman?

30:02.885 --> 30:04.721
Not particularly.

30:06.139 --> 30:07.932
Why don't you turn her over to me?

30:08.016 --> 30:10.518
- Why would I?
- — I agree these people are liars,

30:10.601 --> 30:12.937
and they're certainly
not here to rescue us.

30:13.021 --> 30:16.691
But if I return safely with Charlotte,
they'll take me to the ship.

30:16.774 --> 30:20.194
It's our best chance of finding out
who they are and what they want.

30:20.278 --> 30:23.197
Well, then, I can save you
a lot of trouble, Sayid,

30:23.281 --> 30:26.117
because Ben says
he's got a spy on the boat.

30:29.162 --> 30:30.747
It's a secret.

30:32.040 --> 30:35.710
Forgive me, but the day I start
trusting him is the day I sold my soul.

30:37.045 --> 30:40.131
Give me Charlotte,
allow me to do things my way,

30:40.214 --> 30:43.718
or a war is coming which we
will both be powerless to stop.

30:43.801 --> 30:46.054
Why would I give you Charlotte
for nothing?

30:46.137 --> 30:48.431
I think you misunderstood me.

30:48.514 --> 30:51.392
I never expected you
to give her to me for nothing.

30:56.814 --> 30:59.525
[Soft rock music playing]

31:08.951 --> 31:11.788
Should we get dressed? — no.

31:14.207 --> 31:18.002
We're gonna have to get out
of this bed at a certain point.

31:19.170 --> 31:20.505
Why?

31:21.631 --> 31:24.092
Well, for one thing, because I know

31:24.175 --> 31:28.554
that eventually you're gonna have to go
to that job of yours, you know?

31:28.638 --> 31:31.557
The one you never talk about.

31:31.641 --> 31:34.227
There's nothing to talk about.
It's just a job.

31:37.855 --> 31:39.982
I know nothing about you.

31:42.568 --> 31:45.279
I understand you don't want
to talk about the crash,

31:45.363 --> 31:46.864
what happened to you.

31:49.575 --> 31:51.244
What about you?

31:51.327 --> 31:54.539
It's what you do
when you're in love, right? You...

31:58.543 --> 31:59.877
Inlove?

32:24.569 --> 32:26.237
No more secrets.

32:30.741 --> 32:32.034
What do you want to know?

32:33.077 --> 32:35.830
[Beeping]

32:39.167 --> 32:41.669
He's here. My boss.

32:41.752 --> 32:44.964
I... I have to go.

32:57.185 --> 32:58.186
My dress.

33:12.450 --> 33:14.285
You have to leave Berlin.

33:17.288 --> 33:19.874
You can't be here anymore.
— what do you mean?

33:19.957 --> 33:23.002
- Why would I...?
- — people will be asking questions soon,

33:23.085 --> 33:25.338
about what happened to your employer.

33:27.632 --> 33:30.009
And you can't be around
to answer them.

33:34.347 --> 33:35.640
My employer?

33:40.102 --> 33:42.230
This is about my boss?

33:46.234 --> 33:48.402
Who are you?
— It had nothing to do with...

33:48.486 --> 33:52.114
The café?
You meant to meet me there?

33:55.117 --> 33:58.246
You used me to get to my boss.
What did you say?

33:58.329 --> 34:00.248
People will ask
what happened to him?

34:00.331 --> 34:03.000
It's best you don't know.
— you're gonna kill him?

34:07.255 --> 34:09.257
You're gonna kill him?

34:10.132 --> 34:12.134
Do you even know him?

34:13.052 --> 34:15.721
His name is on a list.
— a list? What list?

34:15.805 --> 34:18.015
You have a list.
— It's my employer's.

34:18.099 --> 34:20.268
Who is that?
— It doesn't matter who he is!

34:20.351 --> 34:23.562
You kill people 'cause they're
on a list? Innocent people?

34:23.646 --> 34:26.357
The man you're working for
is not an economist.

34:39.954 --> 34:41.956
[Dialing phone]

34:42.039 --> 34:45.334
[Speaking German]

35:10.609 --> 35:12.278
What do you think you're...?

35:13.446 --> 35:16.115
[Elsa gasps]

36:05.956 --> 36:09.043
Hey, I'm gonna ask you one last time.

36:09.126 --> 36:11.128
Why was Naomi
carrying this picture of me?

36:11.212 --> 36:14.965
You gotta understand something,
she was senior management.

36:15.049 --> 36:16.258
She stayed on her own.

36:16.342 --> 36:18.677
Naomi told me you people
were hired by her.

36:19.970 --> 36:23.057
So you look me right in the eye
and tell me

36:23.140 --> 36:26.143
you've never seen or heard
of Penelope Widmore.

36:35.403 --> 36:37.780
Fine. You don't want to tell me
the truth?

36:37.863 --> 36:39.448
I'll find someone who will.

36:39.532 --> 36:41.992
See, when that takes off, I'm on it.

37:09.228 --> 37:12.356
Where's Kate?
— she decided to stay.

37:19.530 --> 37:21.699
What happened to miles?
— I traded him.

37:21.782 --> 37:24.452
Traded him?
— I promised you Charlotte. Here she is.

37:27.580 --> 37:29.457
You cheated. — did I?

37:29.540 --> 37:30.958
Yes, you did.

37:31.041 --> 37:33.794
Lucky for you that guy's nothing
but a pain in my ass.

37:35.921 --> 37:37.047
Hey. — hey.

37:37.131 --> 37:40.468
All right. That gives us room
for one more.

37:40.551 --> 37:41.969
Charlotte?

37:42.052 --> 37:45.264
Go back? With all the fun
I'm having here? No.

37:46.265 --> 37:47.600
I've got work to do.

37:48.809 --> 37:50.978
Seat's yours if you want it, Daniel.

37:51.061 --> 37:55.065
No, thank you. I think I should
probably stay with Charlotte.

37:56.525 --> 37:57.735
All right.

38:01.739 --> 38:03.824
Just... just one thing.

38:06.076 --> 38:09.997
Just be sure that you follow
the same exact bearing

38:10.080 --> 38:13.000
that we came in on, ok?
No matter what.

38:13.083 --> 38:16.921
By that I mean no matter what.
Just... stay on it.

38:18.464 --> 38:19.465
Roger that.

38:29.225 --> 38:30.225
Be careful.

38:30.267 --> 38:32.436
I don't have to talk you out of coming.

38:32.520 --> 38:35.731
As much as I like helicopter rides,
you got this one under control.

38:37.733 --> 38:40.236
Wish me luck. — good luck.

38:42.279 --> 38:43.822
Send me a postcard.

38:47.076 --> 38:48.953
You said we have room for one more?

38:50.037 --> 38:51.372
Yeah. Why?

38:53.624 --> 38:55.292
We should bring Naomi home.

40:36.393 --> 40:37.728
[Man] Take your shirt off.

41:07.257 --> 41:09.009
Why didn't she kill you?

41:12.429 --> 41:14.640
She was trying to get
information from me.

41:15.516 --> 41:17.226
[Man] What sort of information?

41:22.981 --> 41:25.401
She wanted to know who I worked for.

41:27.069 --> 41:29.279
She wanted to know about you.

41:30.072 --> 41:31.490
[Man] Of course she did.

41:35.786 --> 41:37.663
Why are you crying?
Because it hurts,

41:37.746 --> 41:40.332
or because you were
stupid enough to care for her?

41:43.419 --> 41:46.171
These people
don't deserve our sympathies.

41:46.964 --> 41:49.758
Need I remind you what they did
the last time you thought

41:49.842 --> 41:52.886
with your heart instead of your gun?

41:52.970 --> 41:55.681
You used that to recruit me
into killing for you.

41:55.764 --> 41:58.559
Do you want to protect
your friends or not, Sayid?

42:04.356 --> 42:06.358
I have another name for you.

42:10.988 --> 42:12.990
But they know I'm after them now.
